# Conformance probe pack for absent-value sentinels (spec 0.9) on the fixed
# `bits` wire, least-significant-bit-first. Public. No kinds. Exercises the
# order of `swap` and the sentinel check (ruling 2: the raw value is read
# after `swap`), sentinels on fields that are not byte aligned, and NaN and
# infinity bit patterns of `f32` as sentinels, where without the sentinel the
# value would be `transform-decode` (ruling 23 of 0.5).
#
#   bytes 0-1    x, 16 bits with `swap` (big-endian in this lsb pack), absent 0x1234
#   bytes 2-3    y, 12 bits from bit 16, absent 0xfff; z, 4 bits from bit 28, absent 10
#   bytes 4-7    ratio, little-endian single, absent 0x7fc00000 (a quiet NaN)
#   bytes 8-11   ce, big-endian single (`swap`), absent 0xffc00000 (a negative quiet NaN)
format     conformance-absent-bits-lsb
version    0.9.0
distribution public
source  "goat-transformers spec/engine-spec.md (synthetic probe format, no external standard)"
uses       probe
wire       bits
word_bytes 1
bit_order  lsb
field   probe.x      0:0:16   uint  swap  absent 4660
field   probe.y      0:16:12  uint  absent 4095
field   probe.z      0:28:4   uint  absent 10
field   probe.ratio  0:32:32  f32   absent 2143289344
field   ce           0:64:32  f32   swap  absent 4290772992
